  "details": "so i've been messing around with the new advanced contact parameters but i keep bumping into walls already between what's possible with material contacts vs what's accessible in the animator, primarly for the data that is captured but not sent to the animator.\n\nSender rotation seems foundamental enough that it's weird we can't access them already, so i think those are critically missing:\n\n_SenderLocalRotationX\n\n_SenderLocalRotationY\n\n_SenderLocalRotationZ\n\n_SenderLocalRotationW (maybe? or is euler rotation enough?)\n\n_SenderAngularVelocityMagnitude\n\nNot everything can be done through custom shaders (android doesn't even have them on avatars) so having those parameters would simplify and improve prefabs that uses contacts and open up new possibilities, such as more believable contact based sound effects, or a better use of built-in avatar contacts so we wouldn't need extra contacts to send rotation informations or other hacks.",
